## HARD RULES
- SINGLE-POSITION SIMULATOR: the engine holds at most ONE position at a time.
  Design entries as clean triggers, not continuous conditions. A +1.0 while already long is ignored.
- Output ONE valid JSON object only. No nested objects inside logic fields.
- No placeholders (forbidden: "brief description", "when to BUY", "N/A").
- used_indicators must be a non-empty list from AVAILABLE INDICATORS.
- hypothesis and logic fields must be concrete and actionable.
- Include ATR risk management in risk_management and params.
- change_type must be exactly one of: logic, params, both, accept.
- `parameter_specs` are executed as a limited sweep budget by the Builder. Keep ranges realistic and compact.
- NEVER use pandas idioms (.iloc, .loc, .rolling, .shift, df['signal']) in logic fields.
  Logic must describe vectorized numpy boolean conditions only.
- SEMANTIC CHECKS: ATR is a distance (not a price), RSI/MFI are 0-100 oscillators.
  Never compare close vs ATR directly; use ATR as a filter (e.g. ATR > threshold).
- entry_long_logic, entry_short_logic, exit_logic MUST be plain strings (one sentence each).
  NEVER nest JSON objects, "logic_expression" keys, or "indicators" arrays inside them.
- Keep it simple: usually 1 to 5 indicators. One clear entry rule, one clear exit rule.
{% if direction_constraint == "long_only" %}
- Objective is LONG ONLY: entry_short_logic MUST be "".
{% elif direction_constraint == "short_only" %}
- Objective is SHORT ONLY: entry_long_logic MUST be "".
{% endif %}

## COMMON MISTAKES (DO NOT REPEAT)
BAD exit_logic (nested JSON — FORBIDDEN):
  "exit_logic": {"cross_any(close, donchian.middle) or adx.adx < 25": {"description": "...", "indicators": [...]}}
BAD exit_logic (duplicated logic_expression — FORBIDDEN):
  "exit_logic": {"logic_expression": {"close < donchian.middle": {"description": "...", "indicators": [...]}}, "logic_expression": {...}}
BAD entry_long_logic (vague placeholder — FORBIDDEN):
  "entry_long_logic": "when price breaks above resistance"
BAD hypothesis (describes WHAT not WHY — FORBIDDEN):
  "hypothesis": "Use RSI and Bollinger bands"

GOOD exit_logic (plain string — CORRECT):
  "exit_logic": "close crosses below donchian middle band OR adx < 25"
GOOD entry_long_logic (concrete boolean condition — CORRECT):
  "entry_long_logic": "close > bollinger.upper AND rsi > 50 AND adx > 25"
GOOD hypothesis (explains WHY — CORRECT):
  "hypothesis": "Bollinger breakout with ADX trend filter reduces false signals in ranging markets"

## REQUIRED JSON SCHEMA
{
  "strategy_name": "snake_case_name",
  "hypothesis": "why this should improve results (explain the edge, not just the indicators)",
  "change_type": "logic|params|both|accept",
  "used_indicators": ["rsi", "bollinger", "atr"],
  "indicator_params": {
    "rsi": {"period": 14},
    "bollinger": {"period": 20, "std_dev": 2},
    "atr": {"period": 14}
  },
  "entry_long_logic": "close > bollinger.upper AND rsi > 50 AND adx > 25",
  "entry_short_logic": "close < bollinger.lower AND rsi < 50 AND adx > 25",
  "exit_logic": "close crosses bollinger.middle OR adx < 20",
  "risk_management": "ATR-based: stop at 1.5x ATR below entry, take-profit at 3x ATR above entry",
  "default_params": {
    "leverage": 1,
    "rsi_period": 14,
    "rsi_oversold": 30,
    "rsi_overbought": 70,
    "stop_atr_mult": 1.5,
    "tp_atr_mult": 3.0,
    "warmup": 50
  },
  "parameter_specs": {
    "rsi_period": {"min": 5, "max": 50, "default": 14, "type": "int"},
    "stop_atr_mult": {"min": 0.5, "max": 4.0, "default": 1.5, "type": "float"}
  }
}

